From ae6559b75f93a2e2c57a1653c512b19ebbaae98f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C2 finding #2 mitigation: correlation-based proxy detection

Mitigates (does not fully close) the disclosed gap that renaming a
proxy or undeclared-tier variable to an innocuous name defeats both
the declared-name proxy screen (check 2) and the input-authorization
tier screen (check 3) alike.

New check_correlation_based_proxy_detection screens input variable
VALUES instead of NAMES: for each numeric/boolean input variable and
each group present in the sealed channel's estimates, computes a
Pearson correlation between the variable's value and that group's
estimated membership probability across a cohort. A rename alone no
longer defeats detection, since the check never looks at the name at
all.

COHORT-level, same architectural shape as check_statistical_outcome_
equity (dimension 4): correlation is a property of a variable across
many decisions, not one decision in isolation. Depends on dimension 4
(now merged, PR #6/67eea1d) for the sealed-channel cohort data this
check reads. New CohortInputDecision dataclass mirrors CohortDecision
but carries the full input_fields snapshot instead of a single
favorable_outcome bool.

Scope, deliberately narrow: numeric and boolean variables only;
string/categorical variable values are NOT screened this session
(documented as a remaining gap, not silently shipped as solved). NOT
wired into rollup_c2_bias_identification or CFPBRegBLens.c2_rollup()
this session -- a caller may fold its findings into their own
known_bad_variable_names bucket if/when they choose to; the wiring
decision itself is deliberately left open, same posture dimensions
2/3 sat in before a later session wired them into the shipped lens.

10 new tests (Tests/test_c2_correlation_based_proxy_detection.py):
cohort-size gate, renamed numeric proxy caught by value not name,
renamed boolean proxy caught, uncorrelated variable stays clean,
constant-value variable skipped (not flagged/indeterminate), sparse
variable skipped without a dedicated finding, string/None values
never treated as numeric, missing-field-in-some-decisions uses only
present pairs, and every finding carries a human-review disclaimer
rather than reading as a verdict.

Full suite: 446 passed, 6 skipped (BISG live tests, no CENSUS_API_KEY
in this sandbox), run twice back-to-back with zero DB reset in
between. ruff (pinned 0.15.22, matching the CI pin) and bandit -ll
both clean.
